PYCHARM_DEBUG=1 python backup.py --config /opt/backup/config.yaml
0 3 * * * /usr/bin/python3 /opt/backup/backup.py --config /opt/backup/config.yaml >> /var/log/backup.log 2>&1

Frappe mode
===========

Enable native Frappe backups in the configuration:

    frappe:
      enabled: true
      bench_dir: /home/frappe/frappe-bench
      site: erp.testpro.io

The utility runs this command before passing the result through the existing
local storage, remote upload, rotation, and alert pipeline:

    bench --site erp.testpro.io backup --with-files --compress --backup-path <work-dir>

Run the utility as the operating-system user that owns the Bench. The generic
`paths` and `db` sections are ignored while Frappe mode is enabled.

Production installations
========================

- Mautic (`marketing`, `/var/www/mautic`): script in `/opt/mautic-backup`,
  scheduled daily at 03:00 server time. Configured but currently requires
  repair: the job cannot create `/opt/backup/logs` and no local backup directory
  exists at `/var/backups/webapp`.
- Frappe ERP/CRM (`erp.testpro.io`): script in `/opt/backup`, native full-site
  backup with database, site config, public files, and private files. Archives
  are stored locally in `/var/backups/frappe-erp` and uploaded to SharePoint
  `/Frappe/auto`; scheduled daily at 03:00 UTC with seven archives retained.
  Failure alerts are sent through Amazon SES email and Telegram.
